<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/8th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Umayyad conquest of Hispania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/711">711 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Arab conquest of Spain</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Umayyad conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> was the Muslim conquest of most of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberian Peninsula</a> beginning in 711 CE. Forces led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tariq-ibn-ziyad">Tariq ibn Ziyad</a> crossed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> and defeated the Visigothic king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roderic">Roderic</a>, and within a few years most of the peninsula was under Umayyad control. The conquest created <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>, which accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> treat as one of its most enduring legacies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/umayyad-conquest-of-hispania.jpg" alt="Umayyad conquest of Hispania" width="320" height="254" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NACLE based on Image:Iberian_Peninsula_location_map.svg created by NordNordWest · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Conquistaislamicapeninsula2.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
